{
 "schema": "neural-forge-matrix-wave43-xchange-go-gate-v1",
 "generated_at": "2026-08-29T07:54:17Z",
 "authority": "this census MAY close the XCHANGE class, by its own pre-registration, and only in one direction: if EVERY surviving conv site fails the conjunction of G1, G2 and G3 then the class closes, because the three gates are preconditions for the substituted operator being in the class at all and no solve restores what is provably outside it.  A pass at ANY site funds ONE build at the cheapest passing site.  This census never grades a child and never moves a floor.",
 "supersedes": "docs/ATTENTION_SHORTCONV_TRANSLATION_DESIGN_2026-08-01.md (design only, never built) for its direction-B acceptance diagnostics",
 "thresholds": {
  "rho_2_max": {
   "value": 0.5,
   "why": "rho_2 is the share of the conv branch's delta that is PROVABLY outside the linear-value attention class, so sqrt(rho_2) is a lower bound on the installed block's relative error at the site before any solve error is added.  Deletion's relative error at the same site is exactly 1.0.  At rho_2 = 0.50 the substitution's error FLOOR is 0.707 -- within thirty per cent of simply deleting the block -- while costing 3,145,856 parameters that deletion does not spend.  Above that line the operator cannot be argued to be carrying the block's function, and the slate's own deleted falsifier (that substitution preserves strictly more than deletion) is the only thing that would have excused building it"
  },
  "gate_dispersion_max": {
   "value": 0.5,
   "why": "nd = Var[g] / E[g^2] is the share of a gate channel's second moment NOT carried by the point the bilinear expansion is taken about.  At nd = 0.50 the expansion point and the fluctuation carry equal energy, which is exactly where 'expand about the mean' stops being a leading-order statement.  Taken as the MEDIAN over the 1,024 channels, so a handful of wild channels cannot fail a site on their own and a broadly fluctuating gate cannot pass"
  },
  "stage1_band_mass_min": {
   "value": 0.9,
   "why": "a lag head's whole job is to put its probability on ONE relative offset, because the per-lag value maps M_l it feeds are per-lag.  A head with more than a tenth of its mass off its assigned lag is not a lag head, it is a smear, and the design document routes that leak downstream rather than absorbing it"
  },
  "reconstruction_rtol": {
   "value": 0.0001,
   "why": "the linear part plus the covariance remainder must sum back to the fp64 recomputation of the branch delta.  This is not a fit tolerance -- the identity is algebraic and holds to fp64 rounding -- it is set four orders above that floor and many orders below any chunk-order or tap-order error, so it catches a wrong decomposition and nothing else"
  }
 },
